Rust geometry backend and parameter data
=======================================

ReShiki's geometry worker uses cosmolkit-core 0.3.0 from the COSMolKit Rust
implementation, https://github.com/Ameyanagi/COSMolKit.git. The complete Git
revision is pinned in native/geometry/Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock and recorded
in each release's build.json. COSMolKit retains its MIT license and the
copyright of the COSMolKit Contributors; its complete terms are included
by the Rust dependency notice supplements and consolidated distribution.
The geometry adapter and worker integration are original ReShiki code.

COSMolKit implements distance-geometry embedding, MMFF94, MMFF94s, UFF,
atom typing, energy/gradient evaluation, and optimization in Rust. Its Rust
build script reads embedded RDKit parameter/torsion/atomic data to generate
Rust constants. Files named Params.cpp and atomic_data.cpp are data sources
for that generator; no C++ solver or Boost headers are compiled or linked.
Python is used only by separate developer/reference tests. The application
runs from its own executable without a Python or RDKit runtime or downloads.

COSMolKit identifies the parameter/reference origin as RDKit 2026.03.1,
revision 351f8f378f8ad6bbd517980c38896e66bf907af8. The independent ReShiki
comparison reference is RDKit 2026.03.6, revision
0e0d85f4ca34aeae15dfc0f7cf5503bdb0a8e985, https://github.com/rdkit/rdkit.
This reference version is retained in the worker protocol's version field;
it does not identify the Rust backend or original parameter-source revision.
Exact SHA-256 values for
COSMolKit's embedded data are audited by scripts/geometry_source.py and
recorded in release build.json. UFF, atomic data, ETKDGv2, small-ring and
macrocycle torsion files match that RDKit reference. The MMFF source adds
an Id header, and the legacy torsion-v1 file repeats its first pattern.

